hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17372","Haddathana Uthman ibn Umar, akhbarana Shubah, from Abi Jafar, he said I heard Umarah ibn Khuzaymah narrating from Uthman ibn Hunayf, that a blind man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Supplicate Allah to heal me. He said: If you wish I supplicate for you, and if you wish I delay that, and it is better. He said: Supplicate Him. So he ordered him to perform ablution and perfect his ablution, then pray two cycles and supplicate with this supplication: O Allah, I ask You and turn to You by Your Prophet Muhammad, prophet of mercy, O Muhammad, I turn by you to my Lord in this need of mine, so fulfill it for me, O Allah, intercede him for me."
"17373","Haddathana Rawh, he said haddathana Shubah, from Abi Jafar al-Madini, he said I heard Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit narrating from Uthman ibn Hunayf, that a blind man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, supplicate Allah to heal me. He said: If you wish I delay that, and it is better for your Hereafter, and if you wish I supplicate for you. He said: No, rather supplicate Allah for me. So he ordered him to perform ablution and to pray two cycles and to supplicate with this supplication: O Allah, I ask You and turn to You by Your Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), prophet of mercy, O Muhammad, I turn by you to my Lord in this need of mine, so fulfill it, and make me intercede in it and intercede him in me. He said: He used to say this repeatedly, then he said after: I think in it is to make me intercede in it. He said: So the man did, and he recovered."
"17374","Haddathana Muammal, he said haddathana Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, he said haddathana Abu Jafar al-Khatmi, from Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from Uthman ibn Hunayf, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whose sight had gone, then he mentioned the hadith."
"17375","Haddathana Hasan ibn Musa, haddathana Ibn Lahiah, haddathana al-Harith ibn Yazid, from al-Bara ibn Uthman al-Ansari, from Hani ibn Muawiyah al-Sadafi, he narrated to him, he said: I performed pilgrimage in the time of Uthman ibn Affan, so I sat in the mosque of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man was narrating to them, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, then a man came and prayed at this pillar, and hastened before completing his prayer, then he left. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If this one died, he would die with nothing of the religion upon him. A man may lighten his prayer and complete it. He said: So I asked about the man, who he was, so it was said: Uthman ibn Hunayf al-Ansari."
